cellGame: cellGameDataExitBroken (NID 0x9949BF82), A Crack in Time 1.20.

(const char* dirName): the title found its game data corrupt; on a console the system shows "the game data is corrupted"
and then ends the application back to the XMB, so the call does not return control to the title in any useful way.
Here it logs the directory and asks the host to quit through ps3_host_quit() (cellSysutil.c: the same path as the PS-button
quit), returns CELL_OK. ENHANCEMENT NOT included: the system message box (cellMsgDialog is not wired in for it).
ASSUMPTION: the quit is the correct end of the call (documented SDK behaviour, nothing on disc contradicts it).

--- a/libs/system/cellGame.c
+++ b/libs/system/cellGame.c
@@ -829,3 +829,13 @@

     return CELL_OK;
 }
+
+/* ---- patch 7024 ---- */
+extern void ps3_host_quit(const char* why);
+s32 cellGameDataExitBroken(const char* dirName)
+{
+    printf("[cellGame] DataExitBroken('%s'): game data broken, ending the application\n",
+           dirName ? (const char*)(vm_base + (uint32_t)(uintptr_t)dirName) : "<null>");
+    ps3_host_quit("cellGameDataExitBroken");
+    return CELL_OK;
+}
